                          COMMAND ...

PDF imposition toolkit: booklets, n-up, step and repeat, shuffling,
trimming, bleeds, page numbers, stamps, automation sequences and hot
folders.

positional arguments:
  COMMAND
    bleed               define page bleeds (trim and bleed boxes)
    booklet             create a 2-up booklet
    creep               compensate for creep in folded booklets
    delete              delete pages
    duplicate           duplicate pages
    evenodd             separate, reorder or rejoin odd and even pages
    impose              impose in one step: booklets, cut stacks, sequential
                        or step and repeat
    info                show page sizes, boxes, bleeds and recorded commands
    insert              insert blank pages or pages from another PDF
    join                join two pages side by side into one
    manual              impose pages at exact positions described in a
                        layout file
    mask                stick masking tape over areas of pages
    merge-data          variable data merge from a CSV file
    move                move pages within the document
    nup                 place several pages on each sheet (n-up)
    peel                peel off stuck-on text, tape, marks or PDF pages
    replay              repeat the commands recorded in another output
                        (imposition by example)
    resize              adjust page sizes (scale, pad or crop to a size)
    reverse             reverse the order of all pages
    rotate              rotate pages by any angle
    run                 run a saved sequence of commands on one or more PDFs
    sample              create a sample document for testing impositions
    shuffle             reorder (and rotate) pages by a repeating rule
    split               split into parts, process each part differently, and
                        optionally rejoin
    step-repeat         fill sheets with copies of each page
    stick-pdf           stick pages of another PDF onto pages
    text                stick on text and page numbers
    tile                split pages into tiles (or undo a 2-up booklet)
    trim-shift          trim, extend, resize or shift page contents
    watch               hot folder: process PDFs as they arrive

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --version             show program's version number and exit

preferences:
  --units {cm,mm,in,pt}
                        unit for lengths given without a suffix (default:
                        cm)
  --registration {black,cmyk,all}
                        colour for marks and registration-coloured text:
                        black, CMYK, or all separations
  --bleed {use,ignore}  use page bleed boxes when imposing, or ignore them
                        (default: use)
  --pdfx                keep a TrimBox when removing bleeds (PDF/X); to make
                        a PDF/X-4 file, use --conform x-4
  --conform {a-1b,a-2b,a-3b,x-4}
                        save the output as PDF/A (a-1b, a-2b, a-3b: for
                        archiving) or PDF/X-4 (x-4: for printing), made by
                        pdf2iso with Ghostscript, which must be installed
  -q, --quiet           no warnings
  --interface {en,es}   the language of the interface, for this run only (to
                        keep a choice, use the 'interface' command)

Run 'py-pdftools impose COMMAND -h' for help on a command. 'py-pdftools
impose file.pdf' on its own makes a booklet with the default settings.
