.nf
usage: py-pdftools impose merge-data [-h] [--units {cm,mm,in,pt}]
                                     [--registration {black,cmyk,all}]
                                     [--bleed {use,ignore}] [--pdfx]
                                     [--conform {a-1b,a-2b,a-3b,x-4}] [-q]
                                     [--interface {en,es}] [-o OUTPUT]
                                     --data DATA --fields FIELDS
                                     [--separator SEPARATOR]
                                     [--encoding ENCODING] [--master]
                                     [--pages-per-record N] [--strict]
                                     [--records RANGE]
                                     input

Variable data merge: add text, text blocks and pictures to pages using records from a CSV file, either by copying a master document per record or by filling successive pages.

Fields file (TOML). Column values are written as {Column Name}:

    [[text]]
    template = "{Name} - {Company Name}"
    page = 1                       # page within the master / record (default: all)
    position = "top-left"          # see 'text --help' for positions
    x = "2cm"
    y = "2cm"
    font = "Helvetica"
    size = 12
    color = "black"
    rotation = 0

    [[picture]]
    file = "logos.pdf"             # one picture per page
    column = "Logo number"         # page number of the picture to use
    position = "top-right"
    x = "1cm"
    y = "1cm"
    fit = "3x2cm"                  # or scale = 100

    [[block]]                      # a text block, e.g. a mailing label
    width = "8cm"
    height = "4cm"
    position = "bottom-left"
    x = "2cm"
    y = "2cm"
    font = "Helvetica"
    size = 11
    justify = "left"               # left | center | right
    overflow = "scale"             # scale | cut | fail
    warn_below = 50                # warn if text is scaled below this percent
    rotation = 0
    lines = [
      { text = "{Title}" },
      { text = "{First name}" },
      { text = "{Last name}", same_line = true },
      { text = "{Address 1}", close_gap = true },
      { text = "{Address 2}", close_gap = true, justify = "right", size = 9 },
    ]

positional arguments:
  input                 source PDF

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  -o, --output OUTPUT   output PDF (default: <input>-<command>.pdf)
  --data DATA           data source: CSV/TSV with a header row
  --fields FIELDS       fields file (TOML); see the description
  --separator SEPARATOR
                        column separator: auto, ',', ';', 'tab'
  --encoding ENCODING   text encoding of the data (default: utf-8-sig)
  --master              the document is a master copied once per record
                        (otherwise records are added to successive groups of
                        pages)
  --pages-per-record N  without --master: pages used by each record
                        (default: 1)
  --strict              fail if records and pages don't match exactly
  --records RANGE       records to use, e.g. 1-10

preferences:
