                              [--background-mode {repeat,once,repeat-last}]
                              [--background-repeat-last N]
                              [--flow {normal,double,double-flip}]
                              input

Combine pages onto larger sheets in rows and columns, with margins, spacing, alignment, crop marks and backgrounds.

positional arguments:
  input                 source PDF

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  -o, --output OUTPUT   output PDF (default: <input>-<command>.pdf)
  --paper SIZE          sheet size: a0, a1, a2, a3, a4, a5, a6, b4, b5,
                        executive, ledger, legal, letter, max, sra3,
                        statement, tabloid, or WxH such as 21x29.7cm
                        (default: a4)
  --orientation {tall,wide,portrait,landscape,best,as-is}
                        sheet orientation (default: best)
  --cols COLS           columns per sheet (maximum, or exact with --scale
                        fit)
  --rows ROWS           rows per sheet (maximum, or exact with --scale fit)
  --scale MODE          'none' (100%), 'fit' (scale so exactly --cols x
                        --rows fit, based on the first page) or a percentage
                        like 50 (default: none)
  --trim                remove unused space at the edge of each sheet (sheet
                        shrinks to the pages plus margins)
  --margin LEN          margin on all four sides (default: 0)
  --margin-top LEN      top margin (overrides --margin)
  --margin-bottom LEN   bottom margin (overrides --margin)
  --margin-left LEN     left margin (overrides --margin)
  --margin-right LEN    right margin (overrides --margin)
  --spacing LEN         space between rows and columns (default: 0)
  --hspace LIST         horizontal spacing between columns; a list like '0
                        40' repeats (overrides --spacing)
  --vspace LIST         vertical spacing between rows; a list repeats
                        (overrides --spacing)
  --align {top-left,top,top-right,left,center,right,bottom-left,bottom,bottom-right}
                        where pages sit on sheets that aren't full (default:
                        top-left)
  --align-sheets-independently
                        align each sheet on its own instead of matching all
                        sheets
  --align-rows          also align each row horizontally (short rows)
  --mirror {none,h,v,hv}
                        mirror margins and alignment on even (back) sheets:
                        horizontally, vertically or both
  --flow {normal,double,double-flip}
                        normal: fill each sheet in turn; double: alternate
                        front/back sheets with backs mirrored; double-flip:
                        as double, with backs upside down (default: normal)

